.TH SNIPPER 1 "2026" "Snipper" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
snipper \- screen capture and annotation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B snipper
.RB [ \-\-region | \-\-full ]
.RB [ \-\-clipboard ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-delay ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B snipper
captures a region of the screen or the whole of it, and opens the result in an
editor where it can be annotated, copied to the clipboard or saved.
.PP
Started without a switch it shows its window. The switches exist so that a
desktop keyboard shortcut can be bound to a capture: an application cannot
register a system-wide hotkey under Wayland, so the desktop's own shortcut
editor is pointed at
.B snipper \-\-region
instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-region
Capture a region chosen by dragging a rectangle.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-full ", " \-\-fullscreen
Capture the whole screen.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-clipboard
Put the capture on the clipboard and quit without showing a window. Needs
.B \-\-region
or
.BR \-\-full .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-delay
Ignore the capture delay set in the interface.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the switches and exit.
.PP
A switch that is not understood is reported rather than ignored. Arguments that
are not switches are ignored.
.SH BUGS
Report them at
.UR https://github.com/alpinsuite/snipper/issues
.UE .
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://buache.systems/snipper/
.UE
